  "notes": "Neo4j's product-level HTTP API is the Aura API (cloud instance management: create/pause/resize DB instances, snapshots, tenants), which is REST + OAuth2 client-credentials, self-serve on free/trial tiers with lower rate limits (25 req/min) vs paid tiers (125 req/min). Separately, database query access uses Bolt/HTTP via language drivers (not a REST product API), and Neo4j also ships an official local MCP server (neo4j/mcp, downloadable binary) plus a larger community-maintained Neo4j Labs MCP suite (neo4j-contrib/mcp-neo4j) for Cypher query execution against any Neo4j deployment. api_breadth marked \"small\" based on the scope of documented Aura API resources (instances/tenants/projects/snapshots/CMKs); no official endpoint count was found in the pages fetched.",
